  "published": "2026-07-25T16:47:57.973Z",
  "releaseNotes": "TRIAL EDITION - SQL longer than 10,000 characters is rejected (parse() returns -1). Full edition: https://www.sqlparser.com\n\nRelease 4.1.0.6\n\n- [PostgreSQL] Support LATERAL in the FROM clause, e.g.\n  SELECT * FROM t1 LEFT JOIN LATERAL (SELECT * FROM t2 WHERE\n  t1.a = t2.a) x ON true and the comma form\n  FROM t1, LATERAL (subquery) x, plus LATERAL over a\n  set-returning function such as generate_series(...). LATERAL is a\n  reserved keyword (as in PostgreSQL), but remains usable as a column\n  label / alias; a table literally named \"lateral\" must be quoted.\n- [PostgreSQL] Accept a bind variable as the FETCH FIRST/NEXT row\n  count, e.g. FETCH FIRST $2 ROWS ONLY (previously only a literal\n  integer or a parenthesized expression was accepted). Also parses the\n  standalone form SELECT ... WHERE col = $1 FETCH FIRST $2 ROWS ONLY.\n\nDemos: https://github.com/sqlparser/gsp_dotnet/tree/master/gsp_demo_dotnet/src/demos",
